  "body": "## Context\n\nBase fleet audit `alsdmlals4-eng/Base#175` found that OMENWARD's canonical adapter is close to the strict Base v1 thin-adapter contract, but its trusted baseline and project CI are not current.\n\n## P1 findings\n\n- `protected_baseline.commit` is behind current `main` (`da382d52b4490acb8758a1683ea6c9e4f4bf388b`).\n- The canonical Base project-adapter validator workflow is not installed as a required project check.\n- The v9.4.3 finalization SHA must be semantically bound to Base's canonical release finalization.\n\n## Required work\n\n- [ ] wait for Base #175 to merge and pin its trusted merged validator commit;\n- [ ] refresh the adapter baseline against the exact PR base;\n- [ ] recompute protected-policy and project Registry hashes;\n- [ ] install the exact-SHA Base validation workflow;\n- [ ] run the full operating-contract validator with the PR base SHA;\n- [ ] preserve OMENWARD canon, product files, and Google Sheets unless separately approved;\n- [ ] keep unexecuted runtime/human gates as `NOT_RUN`.\n\n## Exit condition\n\nOne isolated Draft PR with exact-head CI green, zero unresolved threads, and no Base Skill body copied into the project.",
